    Calls GET /api/v2/product/{code}.

    .PARAMETER Code
    The barcode of the product to be fetched

    .PARAMETER ProductType
    Used for READ queries for one product. Expected product type of the requested product. Defaults to the product type of the server the query is sent to (e.g. 'food' for Open Food Facts, 'beauty' for Open Beauty Facts, etc.). 'all' matches all product types. If the product exists on a different server that matches the requested product type, the API will return a 302 redirect to the correct server. Otherwise, the API will return a 404 error. It is possible that new product types will be added in the future.

    Allowed values: all, beauty, food, petfood, product.
    Sent as 'product_type'.

    .PARAMETER Cc
    2 letter code of the country of the user. Used for localizing some fields in returned values (e.g. knowledge panels). If not passed, the country may be inferred by the IP address of the request.

    .PARAMETER Lc
    2 letter code of the language of the user.
    Used for localizing some fields in returned values (e.g. knowledge panels).
    If not passed, the language may be inferred by the domain name prefix.


    .PARAMETER Fields
    Specific fields to return. Use 'knowledge_panels' for Knowledge Panels only.

    .PARAMETER KnowledgePanelClient
    Client requesting knowledge panels. Used to customize which knowledge panels are returned. Example values: "web", "mobile". Defaults to "app" for all API requests, and "web" for all other requests.
    Sent as 'knowledge_panel_client'.

    .PARAMETER ActivateKnowledgePanelsSimplified
    If true, knowledge panels will include the simplified_root knowledge panel its simplified sub-panels (e.g. simplified health and environment cards)
    Sent as 'activate_knowledge_panels_simplified'.

    .PARAMETER ActivateKnowledgePanelPhysicalActivities
    If true, knowledge panels will include the physical activities panel
    Sent as 'activate_knowledge_panel_physical_activities'.

    .PARAMETER KnowledgePanelsIncluded
    When knowledge_panels are requested, you can specify which panels should be in the response. All the others will be excluded.

    Sent as 'knowledge_panels_included'.

    .PARAMETER KnowledgePanelsExcluded
    When knowledge_panels are requested, you can specify which panels to exclude from the response. All the others will be included.
    If a panel is both excluded and included (with the knowledge_panels_excluded parameter), it will be excluded.

    Sent as 'knowledge_panels_excluded'.

    .PARAMETER Blame
    Include blame information in the response showing who last modified each field of the product.
    The blame information contains the user ID, timestamp, revision number, and value for each field.
    Set to a non-empty and non-0 value (e.g. 1 or true) to enable.


    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

