    .PARAMETER Password
    Password for login
    A SecureString (see ConvertTo-SecureString); it is converted to text only to build the request.

    .PARAMETER InputObject
    A hashtable or object whose properties are sent as the request body. Keys may be this command's parameter names or the API's own property names.
    All piped input is received here, so one command can process many requests from the pipeline.
    Individually specified parameters override matching keys.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    New-OpenFoodFactsSession -UserId 'example' -Password (Read-Host -AsSecureString)

    .LINK
    POST /cgi/session.pl
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory, ParameterSetName = 'Properties')]
        [Alias('user_id')]
        [string]$UserId,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ParameterSetName = 'Properties')]
        [securestring]$Password,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ParameterSetName = 'InputObject', ValueFromPipeline)]
        [object]$InputObject,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('InputObject'))
        {
            $propertyMap = @{
                UserId   = 'user_id'
                Password = 'password'
            }
            $body = ConvertTo-OpenApiBodyTable -InputObject $InputObject -PropertyMap $propertyMap
        } else
        {
            $body = [ordered]@{}
        }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('UserId')) { $body['user_id'] = $UserId }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Password')) { $body['password'] = [System.Net.NetworkCredential]::new('', $Password).Password }
        foreach ($required in @('user_id', 'password'))
        {
            if (-not $body.Contains($required))
            {
                throw "New-OpenFoodFactsSession: the request is missing required property '$required'."
            }
        }

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'POST'
            PathTemplate = '/cgi/session.pl'
            Body         = $body
            BodyType     = 'form'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}

function Search-OpenFoodFactsProduct
{
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Search Products

    .DESCRIPTION
    Search request allows you to get products that match your search criteria.

    It allows you create many custom APIs for your use case.

    If a search query parameter has multiple values, separate them with commas (`,`).
    When filtering with a language-specific parameter (`fr`, `de`, `en`, etc.),
    specify the language code in the parameter name (for example: `categories_tags_en`).

    **Important:** search API v2 does not support full text request (search_term),
    you have to use [search API v1](https://wiki.openfoodfacts.org/API/Read/Search) for that.
    Upcoming [search-a-licious project](https://github.com/openfoodfacts/search-a-licious) will fix that.

    ### Limiting results

    You can limit the size of returned objects thanks to the `fields` object (see below).

    Example: `fields=code,product_name,brands,attribute_groups`

    Please use it as much as possible to avoid overloading the servers.

    The search endpoint uses pagination: see `page` and `page_size` parameters.

    **Beware:** `page_count` is the number of products returned in the current page, not the total number of pages.

    ### Conditions on tags

    All `_tags`` parameters accepts either:

    * a single value
    * or a comma-separated list of values (doing a AND)
    * or a pipe separated list of values (doing a OR)

    You can exclude terms by using a "-" prefix.

    For taxonomized entries, you might either use the tag id (recommended),
    or a known synonym (without language prefix)

    * `labels_tags=en:organic,en:fair-trade` find items that are fair-trade AND organic
    * `labels_tags=en:organic|en:fair-trade` find items that are fair-trade OR organic
    * `labels_tags=en:organic,en:-fair-trade` find items that are organic BUT NOT fair-trade


    ### Conditions on nutriments

    To get a list of nutrients:

    You can either query on nutrient per 100g (`_100g` suffix)
    or per serving (`serving` suffix).

    You can also add `_prepared_`
    to get the nutrients in the prepared product instead of as sold.

    You can add a comparison operator and value to the parameter name
    to get products with nutrient above or below a value.
    If you use a parameter value it exactly match it.

    * `energy-kj_100g<200` products where energy in kj for 100g is less than 200kj
    * `sugars_serving>10` products where sugar per serving is greater than 10g
    * `saturated-fat_100g=1` products where saturated fat per 100g is exactly 10g
    * `salt_prepared_serving<0.1` products where salt per serving for prepared product is less than 0.1g

    ### Combining filters and pagination (examples)

    1. Breakfast cereals with Nutri-Score A or B, with explicit pagination:
       `/api/v2/search?categories_tags_en=breakfast-cereals&nutrition_grades_tags=a|b&page=2&page_size=20&fields=code,product_name,nutrition_grades`

    2. Multiple constraints in one query (category + nutrients + sorting + compact fields):
       `/api/v2/search?categories_tags_en=orange-juices&sugars_100g%3C8&salt_100g%3C0.2&sort_by=last_modified_t&page=1&page_size=24&fields=code,product_name,nutriments`

    3. Include/exclude tags together:
       `/api/v2/search?labels_tags=en:organic,en:-fair-trade&page=1&page_size=24&fields=code,product_name,labels_tags`

    ### Response structure at a glance

    A successful response contains:

    * `count`: total number of matching products
    * `page`: current page number
    * `page_size`: requested number of products per page
    * `page_count`: number of products actually returned in this page
    * `skip`: number of products skipped before this page
    * `products`: array of products for the current page

    Total page count can be computed with:
    `Math.floor((count - 1) / page_size) + 1`

    ### More references

    See also [wiki page](https://wiki.openfoodfacts.org/Open_Food_Facts_Search_API_Version_2)

    Calls GET /api/v2/search.

    .PARAMETER AdditivesTags
    The additives_tags in english of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/additives) has a list of possible values for `additives`. Translated values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/additives.json

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'additives_tags'.

    .PARAMETER AllergensTags
    The allergens_tags in english of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/allergens) has a list of possible values for `allergens`. Translated values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/allergens.json

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'allergens_tags'.

    .PARAMETER BrandsTags
    The brands_tags of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/brands) has a list of possible values for `brands`. Taxonomized values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/brands.json

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'brands_tags'.

    .PARAMETER CategoriesTags
    The category of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/categories) has a list of possible values for `categories`. Translated values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/categories.json

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'categories_tags'.

    .PARAMETER CountriesTagsEn
    The countries_tags_en of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/countries) shows a list of possible values for `countries`. Translated values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/countries.json

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'countries_tags_en'.

    .PARAMETER EmbCodesTags
    The emb_codes_tags of product(s) you are searching for.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'emb_codes_tags'.

    .PARAMETER LabelsTags
    The labels_tags in english of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/labels) has a list of possible values for `labels`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'labels_tags'.

    .PARAMETER ManufacturingPlacesTags
    The manufacturing_places_tags of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/manufacturing-places) has a list of possible values for `manufacturing-places`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'manufacturing_places_tags'.

    .PARAMETER NutritionGradesTags
    The nutrition_grades_tags of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/nutrition-grades) has a list of possible values for `nutrition-grades`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'nutrition_grades_tags'.

    .PARAMETER OriginsTags
    The origins_tags of product(s) you are searching for. The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/origins) has a list of possible values for `origins`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'origins_tags'.

    .PARAMETER PackagingTagsDe
    The packaging_tag in german of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/packaging) has a list of possible values for `packaging`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'packaging_tags_de'.

    .PARAMETER PurchasePlacesTags
    The purchase_places_tags of product(s) you are searching for.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'purchase_places_tags'.

    .PARAMETER StatesTags
    The states_tags in english of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/states) has a list of possible values for `states`. Translated values are available at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/states.json
    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'states_tags'.

    .PARAMETER StoresTags
    The stores_tags of product(s) you are searching for.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'stores_tags'.

    .PARAMETER TracesTags
    The traces_tags of product(s) you are searching for.
    The [Open Food Facts Web App](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/facets/traces) shows a list of possible values for `traces`.

    You can use multiple values by using a comma separated list.
    You can add a "-" before values to avoid matching a tag.

    Sent as 'traces_tags'.

    .PARAMETER TagNameTagsLanguageCode
    You can add a language code to a specific tag to query it in a specific language

    Sent as '<tag_name>_tags_<language_code>'.

    .PARAMETER NutrientLtValue
    Search on nutrient lower than a value

    Sent as '<nutrient>_lt_<value>'.

    .PARAMETER NutrientGtValue
    Search on nutrient greater than a value

    Sent as '<nutrient>_gt_<value>'.

    .PARAMETER NutrientEqValue
    Search on nutrient for an exact quantity

    Sent as '<nutrient>_eq_<value>'.

    .PARAMETER Fields
    Specific fields to return. Use 'knowledge_panels' for Knowledge Panels only.

    .PARAMETER SortBy
    The allowed values  used to sort/order the search results.

    * `product_name` sorts on name
    * `ecoscore_score`, `nova_score`, `nutriscore_score` rank on the [Eco-Score](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/eco-score-the-environmental-impact-of-food-products), [Nova](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/nova), or [Nutri-Score](https://world.openfoodfacts.org/nutriscore)
    * `scans_n`, `unique_scans_n` and `popularity_key` are about product popularity: number of scans on unique scans, rank of product
    * `created_t`, `last_modified_t`, are about creation and modification dates
    * `nothing`, tells not to sort at all (because if you do not provide the sort_by argument we default to sorting on popularity (for food) or last modification date)

    Allowed values: product_name, last_modified_t, scans_n, unique_scans_n, created_t, completeness, popularity_key, nutriscore_score, nova_score, nothing, ecoscore_score.
    Sent as 'sort_by'.

    .PARAMETER Page
    The page number you request to view (eg. in search results spanning multiple pages)


    .PARAMETER PageSize
    The number of elements should be sent per page

    Sent as 'page_size'.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    Search-OpenFoodFactsProduct

    .OUTPUTS
    OpenFoodFacts.SearchForProducts

    .LINK
    GET /api/v2/search
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    [OutputType('OpenFoodFacts.SearchForProducts')]
    param(
        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('additives_tags')]
        [string]$AdditivesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('allergens_tags')]
        [string]$AllergensTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('brands_tags')]
        [string]$BrandsTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('categories_tags')]
        [string]$CategoriesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('countries_tags_en')]
        [string]$CountriesTagsEn,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('emb_codes_tags')]
        [string]$EmbCodesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('labels_tags')]
        [string]$LabelsTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('manufacturing_places_tags')]
        [string]$ManufacturingPlacesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('nutrition_grades_tags')]
        [string]$NutritionGradesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('origins_tags')]
        [string]$OriginsTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('packaging_tags_de')]
        [string]$PackagingTagsDe,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('purchase_places_tags')]
        [string]$PurchasePlacesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('states_tags')]
        [string]$StatesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('stores_tags')]
        [string]$StoresTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('traces_tags')]
        [string]$TracesTags,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [object]$TagNameTagsLanguageCode,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [object]$NutrientLtValue,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [object]$NutrientGtValue,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [object]$NutrientEqValue,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [ValidatePattern('^[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+(,[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)*$', Options = 'None')]
        [string]$Fields,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('sort_by')]
        [ValidateSet('product_name', 'last_modified_t', 'scans_n', 'unique_scans_n', 'created_t', 'completeness', 'popularity_key', 'nutriscore_score', 'nova_score', 'nothing', 'ecoscore_score')]
        [string]$SortBy,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$Page,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('page_size')]
        [int]$PageSize,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        $query = [ordered]@{}
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AdditivesTags')) { $query['additives_tags'] = $AdditivesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AllergensTags')) { $query['allergens_tags'] = $AllergensTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('BrandsTags')) { $query['brands_tags'] = $BrandsTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('CategoriesTags')) { $query['categories_tags'] = $CategoriesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('CountriesTagsEn')) { $query['countries_tags_en'] = $CountriesTagsEn }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('EmbCodesTags')) { $query['emb_codes_tags'] = $EmbCodesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('LabelsTags')) { $query['labels_tags'] = $LabelsTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('ManufacturingPlacesTags')) { $query['manufacturing_places_tags'] = $ManufacturingPlacesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('NutritionGradesTags')) { $query['nutrition_grades_tags'] = $NutritionGradesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('OriginsTags')) { $query['origins_tags'] = $OriginsTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('PackagingTagsDe')) { $query['packaging_tags_de'] = $PackagingTagsDe }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('PurchasePlacesTags')) { $query['purchase_places_tags'] = $PurchasePlacesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('StatesTags')) { $query['states_tags'] = $StatesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('StoresTags')) { $query['stores_tags'] = $StoresTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('TracesTags')) { $query['traces_tags'] = $TracesTags }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('TagNameTagsLanguageCode')) { $query['<tag_name>_tags_<language_code>'] = $TagNameTagsLanguageCode }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('NutrientLtValue')) { $query['<nutrient>_lt_<value>'] = $NutrientLtValue }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('NutrientGtValue')) { $query['<nutrient>_gt_<value>'] = $NutrientGtValue }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('NutrientEqValue')) { $query['<nutrient>_eq_<value>'] = $NutrientEqValue }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Fields')) { $query['fields'] = $Fields }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('SortBy')) { $query['sort_by'] = $SortBy }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Page')) { $query['page'] = $Page }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('PageSize')) { $query['page_size'] = $PageSize }

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'GET'
            PathTemplate = '/api/v2/search'
            Query        = $query
            ResultType   = 'OpenFoodFacts.SearchForProducts'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}

function Send-OpenFoodFactsProductImage
{
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Upload Product Image

    .DESCRIPTION
    Photos are source and proof of data.
    The first photo uploaded for a product is
    auto-selected as the product’s “front” photo.'

    Calls POST /cgi/product_image_upload.pl.

    .PARAMETER Code
    Barcode of the product


    .PARAMETER Imagefield
    Indicates the type of the image and the corresponding language. It should
    be in the format `{IMAGE_TYPE}_{LANG}` format, where `IMAGE_TYPE` is one
    of `front|ingredients|nutrition|packaging` and `LANG` is the 2
    letter language code. Use `other` with no language code
    if you don't want the image to be selected.
    Note that the first image of a product is always selected as front picture.


    .PARAMETER ImguploadFrontEn
    This field must contain image binary content.
    The format and extension must be one of gif|jpeg|jpg|png|heic.
    This field is dynamic and dependent on the value of imagefield in the
    request body. It wil be imgupload_the value of the imagefield stated
    earlier. For example, if `imagefield=front_en`, the name of this field
    should be `imageupload_front_en`.

    Sent as 'imgupload_front_en'.

    .PARAMETER Comment
    A comment on the contribution. It will be shown in product changes history.
    Adding meaningful comments help moderators and users understand a single product history.


    .PARAMETER AppName
    Name of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_name'.

    .PARAMETER AppVersion
    Version of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_version'.

    .PARAMETER AppUuid
    When an app uses a single user to log its contributions,
    it might be interesting to know which user of the app is providing the information.
    You can use this field to provide an identifier (eg: an sha1 of the username) that's privacy preserving. Make sure that your salt is strong, perfectly random and secret

    In case we have trouble with one of your user, it helps our moderators revert edits.

    Sent as 'app_uuid'.

    .PARAMETER UserAgent
    It is required that you pass a specific User-Agent header when you do an API request.
    But some times it's not possible to modify such a header
    (eg. request using JavaScript in a browser).
    In such cases, you can override it with this parameter.

    Sent as 'User-Agent'.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    Send-OpenFoodFactsProductImage -Code 'example' -Imagefield 'example' -ImguploadFrontEn './file'

    .OUTPUTS
    OpenFoodFacts.AddPhotoToExistingProduct

    .LINK
    POST /cgi/product_image_upload.pl
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    [OutputType('OpenFoodFacts.AddPhotoToExistingProduct')]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Code,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [ValidatePattern('^(((front|ingredients|nutrition|packaging)_[a-z]{2})|other)$', Options = 'None')]
        [string]$Imagefield,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('imgupload_front_en', 'FullName', 'Path')]
        [ValidateScript({ Test-Path -LiteralPath $_ -PathType Leaf })]
        [string]$ImguploadFrontEn,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Comment,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_name')]
        [string]$AppName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_version')]
        [string]$AppVersion,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_uuid')]
        [string]$AppUuid,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$UserAgent,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        $body = [ordered]@{}
        $body['code'] = $Code
        $body['imagefield'] = $Imagefield
        $body['imgupload_front_en'] = (Get-Item -LiteralPath $ImguploadFrontEn)
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Comment')) { $body['comment'] = $Comment }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppName')) { $body['app_name'] = $AppName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppVersion')) { $body['app_version'] = $AppVersion }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppUuid')) { $body['app_uuid'] = $AppUuid }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('UserAgent')) { $body['User-Agent'] = $UserAgent }

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'POST'
            PathTemplate = '/cgi/product_image_upload.pl'
            Body         = $body
            BodyType     = 'multipart'
            ResultType   = 'OpenFoodFacts.AddPhotoToExistingProduct'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}

function Set-OpenFoodFactsProductImageCrop
{
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Select and Crop Image

    .DESCRIPTION
    Cropping is only relevant for editing existing products.
    You cannot crop an image the first time you upload it to the system.

    Calls POST /cgi/product_image_crop.pl.

    .PARAMETER Code
    Barcode of the product.

    .PARAMETER Imgid
    identifier of the image to select, it should be a number

    .PARAMETER Id
    identifier of the selected image field, should be in the format
    `{IMAGE_TYPE}_{LANG}` format, where `IMAGE_TYPE` is one of
    `front|ingredients|nutrition|packaging` and `LANG` is the 2 letter
    language code.
    Note that if you select an image for the main language of the product (ex:
    `ingredients_it` if `it` is the main language), this image will be
    displayed on Product Opener for all languages (ex: on
    `https://fr.openfoodfacts.org`, unless `ingredients_fr` exists).

    Also note that "other" is not a valid image type,
    as it makes no sens to crop an image which is not selected.


    .PARAMETER X1
    X origin coordinate of the crop, it must be lower than x2

    .PARAMETER Y1
    Y origin coordinate of the crop, it must be lower than y2

    .PARAMETER X2
    X end coordinate of the crop, it must be higher than x1

    .PARAMETER Y2
    Y end coordinate of the crop, it must be higher than y1

    .PARAMETER Angle
    angle of the rotation to apply on the selected image.
    passing `90` as value rotate the image 90 degrees counter-clockwise.


    .PARAMETER Normalize
    whether the selected image should be normalized using ImageMagick
    Allowed values: true, false.

    .PARAMETER WhiteMagic
    whether the source image should be white magiced (background removal) using
    ImageMagick.

    Allowed values: true, false.
    Server default: false.
    Sent as 'white_magic'.

    .PARAMETER Comment
    A comment on the contribution. It will be shown in product changes history.
    Adding meaningful comments help moderators and users understand a single product history.


    .PARAMETER AppName
    Name of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_name'.

    .PARAMETER AppVersion
    Version of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_version'.

    .PARAMETER AppUuid
    When an app uses a single user to log its contributions,
    it might be interesting to know which user of the app is providing the information.
    You can use this field to provide an identifier (eg: an sha1 of the username) that's privacy preserving. Make sure that your salt is strong, perfectly random and secret

    In case we have trouble with one of your user, it helps our moderators revert edits.

    Sent as 'app_uuid'.

    .PARAMETER UserAgent
    It is required that you pass a specific User-Agent header when you do an API request.
    But some times it's not possible to modify such a header
    (eg. request using JavaScript in a browser).
    In such cases, you can override it with this parameter.

    Sent as 'User-Agent'.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    Set-OpenFoodFactsProductImageCrop -Code 'example' -Imgid 1 -Id 'example'

    .OUTPUTS
    OpenFoodFacts.ProductImageCrop

    .LINK
    POST /cgi/product_image_crop.pl
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    [OutputType('OpenFoodFacts.ProductImageCrop')]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Code,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$Imgid,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [ValidatePattern('^(front|ingredients|nutrition|packaging)_[a-z]{2}$', Options = 'None')]
        [string]$Id,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$X1,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$Y1,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$X2,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$Y2,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [int]$Angle,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [ValidateSet('true', 'false')]
        [string]$Normalize,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('white_magic')]
        [ValidateSet('true', 'false')]
        [string]$WhiteMagic,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Comment,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_name')]
        [string]$AppName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_version')]
        [string]$AppVersion,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_uuid')]
        [string]$AppUuid,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$UserAgent,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        $body = [ordered]@{}
        $body['code'] = $Code
        $body['imgid'] = $Imgid
        $body['id'] = $Id
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('X1')) { $body['x1'] = $X1 }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Y1')) { $body['y1'] = $Y1 }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('X2')) { $body['x2'] = $X2 }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Y2')) { $body['y2'] = $Y2 }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Angle')) { $body['angle'] = $Angle }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Normalize')) { $body['normalize'] = $Normalize }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('WhiteMagic')) { $body['white_magic'] = $WhiteMagic }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Comment')) { $body['comment'] = $Comment }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppName')) { $body['app_name'] = $AppName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppVersion')) { $body['app_version'] = $AppVersion }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppUuid')) { $body['app_uuid'] = $AppUuid }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('UserAgent')) { $body['User-Agent'] = $UserAgent }

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'POST'
            PathTemplate = '/cgi/product_image_crop.pl'
            Body         = $body
            BodyType     = 'multipart'
            ResultType   = 'OpenFoodFacts.ProductImageCrop'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}

function Set-OpenFoodFactsProductImageRotation
{
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Rotate Image

    .DESCRIPTION
    Although we recommend rotating photos manually and uploading a new version of the image,
    the OFF API allows you to make api calls to automate this process.
    You can rotate existing photos by setting the angle to 90º, 180º, or 270º clockwise.

    Calls GET /cgi/product_image_crop.pl.

    .PARAMETER Code
    Barcode of the product

    .PARAMETER Id
    The 'id' query value.

    .PARAMETER Imgid
    The 'imgid' query value.

    .PARAMETER Angle
    The 'angle' query value.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    Set-OpenFoodFactsProductImageRotation -Code 'example' -Id 'example' -Imgid 'example' -Angle 'example'

    .OUTPUTS
    OpenFoodFacts.RotateAPhoto

    .LINK
    GET /cgi/product_image_crop.pl
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    [OutputType('OpenFoodFacts.RotateAPhoto')]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Code,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Id,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Imgid,

        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Angle,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        $query = [ordered]@{}
        $query['code'] = $Code
        $query['id'] = $Id
        $query['imgid'] = $Imgid
        $query['angle'] = $Angle

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'GET'
            PathTemplate = '/cgi/product_image_crop.pl'
            Query        = $query
            ResultType   = 'OpenFoodFacts.RotateAPhoto'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}

function Update-OpenFoodFactsProduct
{
    <#
    .SYNOPSIS
    Edit Product

    .DESCRIPTION
    This updates a product.

    Note: If the barcode exists then you will be editing the existing product,
    However if it doesn''t you will be creating a new product with that unique barcode,
    and adding properties to the product.

    Calls POST /cgi/product_jqm2.pl.

    .PARAMETER Code
    The barcode of the product to be added or edited

    .PARAMETER ProductType
    The product type is a fundamental separation that tells on which platform the product is made available:
    Open Food Facts, Open Beauty Facts, Open Pet Food Facts or Open Products Facts.

    Each platform has variations on the way it analyses the product.

    Changing the product type moves the product to the new platform.
    It must be done thoughtfully.

    Allowed values: beauty, food, petfood, product.
    Sent as 'product_type'.

    .PARAMETER UserId
    Username to authenticate with

    Note: you must always use the username (and not the email)
    as it is far less brittle.

    Sent as 'user_id'.

    .PARAMETER Password
    Password to authenticate with
    A SecureString (see ConvertTo-SecureString); it is converted to text only to build the request.

    .PARAMETER Lc
    2 letter code of the language of the interface. Used to determine the language of certain fields (e.g. product_name and taxonomy fields like categories and labels). If not passed, the language may be inferred by the country of the user (passed through the cc field or inferred by the IP address). Full list at https://static.openfoodfacts.org/data/taxonomies/languages.json

    .PARAMETER Lang
    2 letter language code of the main language of the product (the most prominent on the packaging)

    .PARAMETER ProductName
    Product name in the language sent in the lc field. For backward compatibility only, use the field product_name_[language_code] instead.
    Sent as 'product_name'.

    .PARAMETER AbbreviatedProductName
    Abbreviated product name. For backward compatibility only, use the field abbreviated_product_name_[language_code] instead.
    Sent as 'abbreviated_product_name'.

    .PARAMETER GenericName
    Legal name of the product. For backward compatibility only, use the field generic_name_[language_code] instead.
    Sent as 'generic_name'.

    .PARAMETER IngredientsText
    Raw list of ingredients text. For backward compatibility only, use the field ingredients_text_[language_code] instead.
    Sent as 'ingredients_text'.

    .PARAMETER PackagingText
    Packaging information text. For backward compatibility only, use the field packaging_text_[language_code] instead.
    Sent as 'packaging_text'.

    .PARAMETER Quantity
    Product quantity with unit

    .PARAMETER Labels
    Product labels (comma-separated list)

    .PARAMETER Categories
    Product categories (comma-separated list)

    .PARAMETER Brands
    Product brands (comma-separated list)

    .PARAMETER Stores
    Stores where product is sold

    .PARAMETER Countries
    Countries where product is sold

    .PARAMETER Origins
    Origins of ingredients

    .PARAMETER Traces
    Traces of allergens

    .PARAMETER Packaging
    Packaging type, format, material.
    The [v3 API documentation](https://openfoodfacts.github.io/openfoodfacts-server/api/ref-v3/#operation/post-api-v3-product-barcode)
    has a more structured data for `packaging`.


    .PARAMETER ServingSize
    Serving size
    Sent as 'serving_size'.

    .PARAMETER NutritionDataPer
    Whether nutrition data is per 100g or per serving. Note that this field applies to all nutriment fields (existing or new). So if its value is changed, all nutrients should be supplied, so that we don't have existing values per 100g when the new values are per serving, or vice versa.
    Allowed values: 100g, serving.
    Sent as 'nutrition_data_per'.

    .PARAMETER Comment
    A comment on the contribution. It will be shown in product changes history.
    Adding meaningful comments help moderators and users understand a single product history.


    .PARAMETER AppName
    Name of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_name'.

    .PARAMETER AppVersion
    Version of the app providing the information

    Sent as 'app_version'.

    .PARAMETER AppUuid
    When an app uses a single user to log its contributions,
    it might be interesting to know which user of the app is providing the information.
    You can use this field to provide an identifier (eg: an sha1 of the username) that's privacy preserving. Make sure that your salt is strong, perfectly random and secret

    In case we have trouble with one of your user, it helps our moderators revert edits.

    Sent as 'app_uuid'.

    .PARAMETER UserAgent
    It is required that you pass a specific User-Agent header when you do an API request.
    But some times it's not possible to modify such a header
    (eg. request using JavaScript in a browser).
    In such cases, you can override it with this parameter.

    Sent as 'User-Agent'.

    .PARAMETER Endpoint
    Base URL of the API. Defaults to the saved/default endpoint (see the *DefaultEndpoint commands).

    .PARAMETER Credential
    Credential for the API; the password is used as the token/key when the API uses one.

    .PARAMETER Headers
    Extra request headers.

    .PARAMETER TimeoutSec
    Request timeout in seconds (default 100).

    .EXAMPLE
    Update-OpenFoodFactsProduct -Code 'example'

    .OUTPUTS
    OpenFoodFacts.AddOrEditAProduct

    .LINK
    POST /cgi/product_jqm2.pl
    #>
    [CmdletBinding()]
    [OutputType('OpenFoodFacts.AddOrEditAProduct')]
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory, ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Code,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('product_type')]
        [ValidateSet('beauty', 'food', 'petfood', 'product')]
        [string]$ProductType,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('user_id')]
        [string]$UserId,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [securestring]$Password,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Lc,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Lang,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('product_name')]
        [string]$ProductName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('abbreviated_product_name')]
        [string]$AbbreviatedProductName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('generic_name')]
        [string]$GenericName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('ingredients_text')]
        [string]$IngredientsText,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('packaging_text')]
        [string]$PackagingText,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Quantity,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Labels,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Categories,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Brands,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Stores,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Countries,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Origins,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Traces,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Packaging,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('serving_size')]
        [string]$ServingSize,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('nutrition_data_per')]
        [ValidateSet('100g', 'serving')]
        [string]$NutritionDataPer,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$Comment,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_name')]
        [string]$AppName,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_version')]
        [string]$AppVersion,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [Alias('app_uuid')]
        [string]$AppUuid,

        [Parameter(ValueFromPipelineByPropertyName)]
        [string]$UserAgent,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidatePattern('^https?://')]
        [string]$Endpoint,

        [Parameter()]
        [System.Management.Automation.Credential()]
        [pscredential]$Credential,

        [Parameter()]
        [hashtable]$Headers,

        [Parameter()]
        [ValidateRange(0, 86400)]
        [int]$TimeoutSec
    )

    process
    {
        $body = [ordered]@{}
        $body['code'] = $Code
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('ProductType')) { $body['product_type'] = $ProductType }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('UserId')) { $body['user_id'] = $UserId }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Password')) { $body['password'] = [System.Net.NetworkCredential]::new('', $Password).Password }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Lc')) { $body['lc'] = $Lc }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Lang')) { $body['lang'] = $Lang }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('ProductName')) { $body['product_name'] = $ProductName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AbbreviatedProductName')) { $body['abbreviated_product_name'] = $AbbreviatedProductName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('GenericName')) { $body['generic_name'] = $GenericName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('IngredientsText')) { $body['ingredients_text'] = $IngredientsText }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('PackagingText')) { $body['packaging_text'] = $PackagingText }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Quantity')) { $body['quantity'] = $Quantity }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Labels')) { $body['labels'] = $Labels }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Categories')) { $body['categories'] = $Categories }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Brands')) { $body['brands'] = $Brands }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Stores')) { $body['stores'] = $Stores }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Countries')) { $body['countries'] = $Countries }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Origins')) { $body['origins'] = $Origins }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Traces')) { $body['traces'] = $Traces }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Packaging')) { $body['packaging'] = $Packaging }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('ServingSize')) { $body['serving_size'] = $ServingSize }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('NutritionDataPer')) { $body['nutrition_data_per'] = $NutritionDataPer }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('Comment')) { $body['comment'] = $Comment }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppName')) { $body['app_name'] = $AppName }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppVersion')) { $body['app_version'] = $AppVersion }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('AppUuid')) { $body['app_uuid'] = $AppUuid }
        if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey('UserAgent')) { $body['User-Agent'] = $UserAgent }

        $request = @{
            ClientInfo   = $Script:OpenFoodFactsClientInfo
            Method       = 'POST'
            PathTemplate = '/cgi/product_jqm2.pl'
            Body         = $body
            BodyType     = 'multipart'
            ResultType   = 'OpenFoodFacts.AddOrEditAProduct'
        }
        foreach ($common in 'Endpoint', 'Credential', 'Headers', 'TimeoutSec', 'OutFile')
        {
            if ($PSBoundParameters.ContainsKey($common))
            {
                $request[$common] = $PSBoundParameters[$common]
            }
        }

        Invoke-OpenApiRequest @request
    }
}
